{"alias":"/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/guidelines","title":"School Health Service","changed":"2026-08-25T17:38:58+00:00","before":"<img alt=\"School Health Service Banner\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"d64223bb-9115-44c3-86b3-a60255e6a154\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/School%20Health%20-%20Service%20Banner.png\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<p><br />\r\nSchool nurses provide emergency care, preventive services (e.g., immunizations, screenings), and coordinate with&nbsp;families and providers to keep students healthy and ready to learn.&nbsp;The <a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"9f6969a7-c250-4397-964b-101f74c42b3c\" filename=\"School Health Services - School Nurse Evaluation Tool - 12.2.2025.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20School%20Nurse%20Evaluation%20Tool%20-%2012.2.2025.pdf\">Maine School Nurse Evaluation Tool: School Nurse Competencies and Evaluation</a>&nbsp;helps guide growth, goal setting, and evaluation, aligning with the <a href=\"https://www.nasn.org/nasn-resources/framework\">NASN School Nursing Practice Framework™.</a> Like teachers and administrators, nurses should be supported through professional development and evaluation systems. School nurses operate within both health and education systems, facing unique legal, policy, and ethical challenges. The <a href=\"https://www.nasn.org/nasn-resources/professional-topics/codeofethics\">NASN Code of Ethics</a> offers guidance for practice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Resources available through Maine DOE and national organizations include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Guidance documents and protocols for student health</li>\r\n\t<li>Professional practice resources for school nurses</li>\r\n\t<li>Additional tools to strengthen school health services\r\n\t<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-left\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8\">\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h5 class=\"card-title\">Guidelines for School Health Services&nbsp;</h5>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"http://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/chronic\">Chronic Conditions Management</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"8192088d-d8d5-441c-beb8-fcd4f54f12b6\" href=\"/doe/node/3615\">Communicable Disease</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"70b34951-1d26-4c20-b883-73568ff262b4\" href=\"/doe/node/320\">Concussion Management</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"http://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/oversight\">Delegation, Coordination, &amp; Oversight</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"7aba3718-08b9-43c2-b82f-c359e2f1195a\" filename=\"School Health Services - Early Childhood Health Resources - 6.10.2026.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Early%20Childhood%20Health%20Resources%20-%206.10.2026.pdf\">Early Childhood Health and Safety</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"6f427f1a-a412-4fc8-864f-e9980b87bffe\" href=\"/doe/node/4421\">Emergency Care</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"node\" data-entity-uuid=\"cc6a6426-69f3-41b6-9565-d63e6704a5cc\" href=\"/doe/node/3721\">Health Screenings</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/immunization\">Immunization</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/medication\">Medication Administration</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schoolsupports/schoolhealth/mentalhealth\">Mental Health and Substance Use Prevention</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schoolsupports/schoolhealth/service/dental\" title=\"Oral Health Resources\">Oral Health</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/pests\" target=\"_self\">Pests in Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><strong>Pandemic Planning</strong><br />\r\n\t&nbsp;\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schoolsafety\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Maine School Safety Center Emergency Management</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.schoolsafety.gov/emergency-planning\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">SchoolSafety.gov: Emergency Planning</a></li>\r\n\t\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/pandemic-flu/php/national-strategy/?CDC_AAref_Val=https://www.cdc.gov/flu/pandemic-resources/national-strategy/index.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">National Pandemic Strategy from US&nbsp;CDC</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/emergency-managers/national-preparedness/training\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) Training</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"person at computer\" data-entity-type=\"file\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-cottonbro-studio-4065876%20%284%29.jpg\